# Trusted ignore policy. Target-owned ignore files are not used, and every
# entry here must be commit-scoped so it can only ever match this
# repository's own history scan, never a target scanned in directory mode.

# 2026-08-24: five history-only entries, all one commit, all the same string.
# The commit that taught the council about giveaway words quoted the live
# false positive (a 19-character sk_test value) in two comments and built it
# in a regression test, and this repository's own history scan flagged all
# five, which is the guard working. The working tree was fixed the same day;
# a commit is immutable, so history needs these fingerprints. They are
# commit-scoped, and the live scanner runs in directory mode where a
# commit-scoped fingerprint can never match, so nothing here can ever
# suppress a finding in a scanned repository.
